Please don't lie to me.

720
01:20:32,417 --> 01:20:37,212
It might've slipped my mind.
But I didn't forget. I remembered....

721
01:20:38,338 --> 01:20:41,883
I didn't remember,
but I didn't forget, okay?

722
01:20:42,091 --> 01:20:45,763
Things get crazy.
It's hard to keep things straight.

723
01:20:45,971 --> 01:20:47,431
I know. I see that.

724
01:20:47,639 --> 01:20:50,351
-It is.
-I know. I see that.

725
01:20:51,478 --> 01:20:54,312
Emily, you look great.

726
01:20:54,813 --> 01:20:58,484
Come on. You're wasted.
You're absolutely wasted.

727
01:20:58,693 --> 01:21:01,821
-No, I'm not wasted. I'm tired.
-Sorry.

728
01:21:02,029 --> 01:21:05,658
I gotta do him first,
because I gotta work at midnight.

729
01:21:05,867 --> 01:21:10,871
Come over here. Stand over here
for a second, all right?

730
01:21:11,080 --> 01:21:12,956
-Who are you?
-Izzy.

731
01:21:13,165 --> 01:21:14,625
What is this? What?

732
01:21:14,833 --> 01:21:18,378
Izzy. But you don't have
to call me that. It's me.

733
01:21:18,796 --> 01:21:21,716
Call me Chrizzy, okay?

734
01:21:21,924 --> 01:21:25,802
You don't have to call me Izz.
Call me Chris.

735
01:21:26,012 --> 01:21:29,765
Chris. Well, I'm glad we talked.
I'm gonna go.

736
01:21:29,974 --> 01:21:32,267
-Emily, wait.
-What? What?

737
01:21:32,684 --> 01:21:37,064
-I'll go with you.
-Go with me where?

738
01:21:38,106 --> 01:21:40,819
With you. I'm gonna go to Seattle.

739
01:21:43,530 --> 01:21:45,907
We're in Seattle, Chrizzy.

740
01:21:50,202 --> 01:21:52,913
Sorry, sorry. But...

741
01:21:53,122 --> 01:21:55,834
...are you guys done?
Because l--

742
01:21:56,042 --> 01:21:57,585
We're done.

743
01:21:58,127 --> 01:22:03,133
Get going on this one because
she's gotta be at work by midnight.

744
01:22:04,800 --> 01:22:06,552
Dinner's canceled.

745
01:22:06,760 --> 01:22:09,680
She's really sweet,
but I was here first.

746
01:22:09,889 --> 01:22:13,434
Why don't we go in here?
Somewhere out of the way.

747
01:22:54,310 --> 01:22:56,312
Can I get a picture, Izzy?

748
01:23:04,861 --> 01:23:07,989
All right, I gotta go.
Here you go.

749
01:23:17,999 --> 01:23:21,544
Jorg, it's not very brutal.
Can we make it more raunchy?

750
01:23:22,170 --> 01:23:23,505
Sounds raunchy in here.

751
01:23:23,714 --> 01:23:27,593
Maybe it's an E.Q. thing.
Just take a few minutes.

752
01:23:28,009 --> 01:23:33,223
It needs a bit of bollocks to it.
E.Q. it or something.

753
01:23:33,639 --> 01:23:35,933
Good hunting at your ranch?

754
01:23:36,142 --> 01:23:40,939
Great. Everything I saw, I killed.
Killed something every damn day.

755
01:23:41,147 --> 01:23:44,151
You should bring
your new fiancée up there.

756
01:23:44,360 --> 01:23:48,029
She's busy at the moment.
Some yearbook committee.

757
01:23:48,322 --> 01:23:49,698
--got any body to it.

758
01:23:49,990 --> 01:23:51,366
-Hey, Izz.
-What's up?

759
01:23:51,574 --> 01:23:54,911
-Hello, Chrizzy.
-How are you guys?

760
01:23:55,120 --> 01:23:58,247
-What's with your eyebrow?
-Isn't it cool?

761
01:23:58,874 --> 01:24:02,294
You gotta clear it with us
before you do that.

762
01:24:06,799 --> 01:24:11,469
Worked on some songs for the album.
They're still rough...

763
01:24:11,677 --> 01:24:15,557
...but I wanted to get your input
before I went further.

764
01:24:15,765 --> 01:24:17,017
I don't know.

765
01:24:17,935 --> 01:24:21,397
Just a thought,
but isn't that a cool cover?

766
01:24:21,606 --> 01:24:25,566
No title, no band name.
Could be heavy. What do you think?

767
01:24:31,072 --> 01:24:33,367
Izzy, it looks great.

768
01:24:33,992 --> 01:24:35,578
It still needs work.

769
01:24:36,078 --> 01:24:38,914
I'm glad you've been having fun
writing songs.

770
01:24:39,956 --> 01:24:42,252
I busted my ass
working on the songs.

771
01:24:42,669 --> 01:24:45,462
But the tunes have
already been written.

772
01:24:46,713 --> 01:24:50,802
-What do you mean?
-A.C. and I wrote them during break.

773
01:24:51,093 --> 01:24:55,597
-I know you and A.C. do most of it--
-Not most. All of it.

774
01:24:55,889 --> 01:24:58,726
But shouldn't I have some input?

775
01:24:59,852 --> 01:25:04,022
I'm singing the tunes,
so you at least want my stamp.

776
01:25:04,232 --> 01:25:05,691
I'm not just....

777
01:25:05,900 --> 01:25:09,987
You aren't just expecting me
to be some singer-for-hire, are you?

778
01:25:13,950 --> 01:25:17,161
Let me explain. Come here.

779
01:25:17,369 --> 01:25:22,291
Listen, our fans, right,
our loyal, die-hard fans...

780
01:25:22,499 --> 01:25:27,297
...our very lifeblood, if you will,
expect to see certain things.

781
01:25:27,505 --> 01:25:29,465
We give them what they want.

782
01:25:29,673 --> 01:25:34,054
We don't deviate because one
disappointed fan can turn into two...

783
01:25:34,262 --> 01:25:37,305
...to four, to eight,
till the next thing you know...

784
01:25:37,515 --> 01:25:39,891
...we're playing to a half-empty hall.

785
01:25:40,226 --> 01:25:45,439
And our lost sheep are off enjoying
the rock stylings of, say, Ratt.

786
01:25:45,856 --> 01:25:50,028
So while I understand your impulse
to do your own thing...

787
01:25:50,236 --> 01:25:53,364
...and I admire it
in some small way...

788
01:25:53,989 --> 01:25:56,159
...if you want to stay
with Steel Dragon...

789
01:25:56,367 --> 01:26:01,580
...then you have to reconcile yourself
to doing the Steel Dragon thing.

790
01:26:01,915 --> 01:26:06,920
All right? And the Steel Dragon thing
is that A.C. and I write the songs.

791
01:26:07,628 --> 01:26:10,966
And you sing the songs that we write.

792
01:26:12,341 --> 01:26:13,801
Am I clear?

793
01:26:14,843 --> 01:26:15,969
Yeah.

794
01:26:16,387 --> 01:26:17,555
Good.

795
01:26:48,836 --> 01:26:50,296
What's he doing?

796
01:26:53,508 --> 01:26:56,344
-What?
-Just sing it like it's written.

797
01:26:56,552 --> 01:26:58,429
-I thought I was.
-You weren't.

798
01:26:59,055 --> 01:27:00,181
All right. Sorry.

799
01:27:00,515 --> 01:27:03,310
-Great.
-Theo, from the top.

800
01:27:04,143 --> 01:27:05,727
Thanks.

801
01:27:27,000 --> 01:27:28,334
Pretty good.

802
01:27:44,518 --> 01:27:48,271
What is it when you do something
to somebody and they hate it?

803
01:27:48,896 --> 01:27:52,442
Then somebody does the same
to you and you hate it.

804
01:27:52,943 --> 01:27:57,446
I suppose some might call it
poetic justice. I don't know.

805
01:28:01,410 --> 01:28:06,415
All I know is I owe a guy named Rob
a big fat apology. That's for sure.

806
01:28:06,624 --> 01:28:11,837
We all owe someone an apology along
the way. I mean, that's life, man.

807
01:28:13,923 --> 01:28:16,299
A long, long time ago...

808
01:28:16,925 --> 01:28:19,427
...when I was at university...

809
01:28:20,262 --> 01:28:22,056
...I was married.

810
01:28:25,684 --> 01:28:28,104
No. You were married?

811
01:28:28,312 --> 01:28:33,733
It was before you boys and that
rock 'n' roll music corrupted me, man.

812
01:28:35,694 --> 01:28:38,947
Yeah, I still think
about it sometimes.

813
01:28:40,615 --> 01:28:44,787
She was really a very sweet girl.

814
01:28:49,875 --> 01:28:53,003
What happened?
If you don't mind me asking.

815
01:28:53,212 --> 01:28:54,587
No, no.

816
01:28:56,465 --> 01:28:59,051
One day we were sitting in the park.

817
01:28:59,259 --> 01:29:02,179
Having lunch, me and the wife.

818
01:29:02,387 --> 01:29:04,890
I needed to take a piss...

819
01:29:05,100 --> 01:29:08,852
...so I walked to the toilet.
You know, in the bathroom.

820
01:29:09,894 --> 01:29:13,774
I'm standing there staring
at the wall, as you do.

821
01:29:15,526 --> 01:29:20,239
And all of the sudden,
something came over me.

822
01:29:21,282 --> 01:29:26,162
Like a fear that my whole life
had already been laid out for me.

823
01:29:27,412 --> 01:29:30,332
I'd finish my studies, get a job.

824
01:29:30,540 --> 01:29:32,836
I'd be working for somebody else...

825
01:29:33,044 --> 01:29:36,589
...worrying about things
that didn't matter.

826
01:29:39,926 --> 01:29:41,928
So I walked out of there.

827
01:29:42,220 --> 01:29:45,972
Kept going. Didn't come back.

828
01:29:48,600 --> 01:29:50,353
You just left her there?

829
01:29:52,021 --> 01:29:53,188
Yep.

830
01:29:54,024 --> 01:29:58,069
Sitting in front of a half-eaten
steak and kidney pie.

831
01:30:01,197 --> 01:30:03,824
Very harsh, man.

832
01:30:05,909 --> 01:30:10,915
She came to see the show a few years
ago. She hadn't changed at all.

833
01:30:12,166 --> 01:30:15,294
She married my best friend.
A doctor.

834
01:30:15,503 --> 01:30:18,714
They have three gorgeous little kids.

835
01:30:21,133 --> 01:30:24,345
Yeah, she's very happy.

836
01:30:25,596 --> 01:30:27,181
Very happy.

837
01:31:13,895 --> 01:31:15,438
Thank you.

838
01:31:16,272 --> 01:31:18,900
You know, I'm just a regular guy...

839
01:31:19,109 --> 01:31:22,446
...who grew up with posters
of these guys on my walls.

840
01:31:22,654 --> 01:31:25,991
And now I'm one of them.
That's right.

841
01:31:26,199 --> 01:31:31,413
I'm standing here, and I'm proof if you
work hard and want it bad enough....

842
01:31:31,621 --> 01:31:33,289
Dreams come true!

843
01:31:33,498 --> 01:31:37,044
That's right. Dreams do come true
so follow them.

844
01:32:41,149 --> 01:32:42,318
Me?

845
01:33:30,700 --> 01:33:32,868
-Awesome!
-What's your name?

846
01:33:33,076 --> 01:33:36,747
Mike, but my friends call me
Thor, God of Thunder!

847
01:33:36,955 --> 01:33:38,917
-Know the rest of it?
-Know them all.

848
01:33:39,125 --> 01:33:42,378
I know all your moves.
I study you. I love you.

849
01:33:42,586 --> 01:33:45,589
You want to rip
the roof off this place?

850
01:33:46,133 --> 01:33:47,383
Are you serious?

851
01:33:48,426 --> 01:33:49,467
Yep.

852
01:33:52,470 --> 01:33:56,559
Go ahead. Get out there.
Get out there, bro. It's all yours.

853
01:35:02,125 --> 01:35:05,460
-Everything all right?
-Couldn't be better.

854
01:35:06,421 --> 01:35:08,506
Taking a night off, are you?

855
01:35:09,966 --> 01:35:12,051
I'm gonna go take a piss.

856
01:35:19,433 --> 01:35:21,019
I'll see you again.

857
01:35:35,700 --> 01:35:37,577
Off you go.

858
01:35:49,673 --> 01:35:53,009
Chris "Izzy" Cole of Steel Dragon
shocked fans...

859
01:35:53,217 --> 01:35:55,428
... when he walked offstage.

860
01:35:55,636 --> 01:35:58,640
Izzy's departure is
more trouble for Steel Dragon...

861
01:35:59,057 --> 01:36:01,893
...as the band tries
to maintain its status...

862
01:36:02,102 --> 01:36:04,689
...as the industry's
top hard-rock act.

863
01:36:04,897 --> 01:36:08,233
As far as I'm concerned,
it's much ado about nothing.

864
01:36:08,442 --> 01:36:12,404
There's still four of us left.
We're not going anywhere.

865
01:36:12,612 --> 01:36:15,740
I don't give a fuck where he is...

866
01:36:15,949 --> 01:36:18,786
...and I don't care if I see
that bastard again.

867
01:36:19,620 --> 01:36:21,496
He said to me:

868
01:36:22,331 --> 01:36:24,499
"I need to take a piss. "

869
01:36:25,250 --> 01:36:26,794
That's it.

870
01:36:27,003 --> 01:36:30,338
"Mats," he said,
"I really need a piss. "

871
01:36:31,089 --> 01:36:34,635
One day I realized
it wasn't for me anymore.

872
01:36:34,843 --> 01:36:38,680
I was wearing the clothes
and singing the songs.

873
01:36:39,932 --> 01:36:42,143
It just didn 't feel right.

874
01:36:42,768 --> 01:36:47,147
I just wanted to find myself.
Find my own music.

875
01:37:28,647 --> 01:37:30,398
-What's up?
-Long time.

876
01:37:30,607 --> 01:37:34,153
-It has been. You cut your hair.
-So did you, asshole.

877
01:37:50,335 --> 01:37:52,004
I'm starting a new band.

878
01:37:52,212 --> 01:37:56,049
I got "Whole and a Half"
on a shelf. It's ready to go.

879
01:39:10,416 --> 01:39:12,585
I'm gonna go talk to Emily.

880
01:39:36,360 --> 01:39:37,820
I missed you.

881
01:39:41,490 --> 01:39:43,366
I know. Me too.

882
01:39:48,997 --> 01:39:52,751
-I wanted to tell you.
-I know.

883
01:39:53,877 --> 01:39:55,337
I know.

884
01:39:57,131 --> 01:39:58,882
You look great.

885
01:40:02,635 --> 01:40:04,721
So do you.

886
01:40:30,080 --> 01:40:32,375
Why didn't you rejoin the band?

887
01:40:32,583 --> 01:40:36,752
As the mouthpiece of Steel Dragon,
I had this responsibility.

888
01:40:38,505 --> 01:40:42,467
It's me they're looking at
and want to learn from.

889
01:40:42,676 --> 01:40:47,598
The vacuous, empty world of sex
and drugs and rock 'n' roll...

890
01:40:47,807 --> 01:40:50,100
...is not the message
I want to send out.

891
01:40:51,976 --> 01:40:56,148
I wanted something more cerebral,
eloquent and dignified.

892
01:41:00,110 --> 01:41:01,362
We kick ass, man!

893
01:41:01,654 --> 01:41:05,115
Ever get your ass kicked by
a guy with long hair and makeup?

894
01:41:05,324 --> 01:41:06,867
Right here!

895
01:41:09,161 --> 01:41:12,205
Chris "Izzy" Cole shocked fans--
Damn it!

896
01:41:12,414 --> 01:41:13,540
Cut!

897
01:41:14,499 --> 01:41:16,877
Okay, Backstage Pass.
Okay, Crud Pollution.

898
01:41:17,086 --> 01:41:20,130
Okay, Bobby Beers.
I mean, Chris Queers.

899
01:41:22,007 --> 01:41:24,093
After the nuclear holocaust...

900
01:41:24,302 --> 01:41:28,888
...survivors will crawl out
of the rubble, light a fire...

901
01:41:29,097 --> 01:41:31,892
...then one man,
the singer of songs, will sing.

902
01:41:32,101 --> 01:41:34,811
And that is the essence
of rock 'n' roll.

903
01:41:35,145 --> 01:41:37,649
What are you talking about?

904
01:41:45,447 --> 01:41:47,115
Chris....

905
01:41:47,324 --> 01:41:50,160
As they continue--
What are they continuing?

906
01:41:50,369 --> 01:41:54,123
As the band continues
to struggle to continue its--

907
01:42:00,797 --> 01:42:01,839
What?

908
01:42:03,924 --> 01:42:05,384
Oh, my God.

909
01:42:34,664 --> 01:42:38,209
No more metal shit.
It's all about hip-hop.

910
01:42:38,417 --> 01:42:41,879
It's all bling-bling, pinky ring,
word about, bling-bling.

911
01:42:42,087 --> 01:42:45,842
No more of this. It's about this.
You heard me?

912
01:42:46,050 --> 01:42:50,097
Lay your shit by the TV and watch
this shit. This shit the bomb.


